PDL_SPECIFICATION_VERSION 0.1.0

STATUS DRAFT

SCOPE

This version defines only the minimal flat grammar needed to read and
write a .pace/ instance's root manifest files (INSTANCE.pdl,
ACTIVE_VERSIONS.pdl) and similarly flat section files. It does not yet
formally define the richer nested prose style used by this repository's
own governance/ontology/contracts documents — those remain human- and
AI-readable, not machine-parsed, until a future version of this
specification covers them.

GRAMMAR

A PDL document is a sequence of lines.

A blank line is ignored.

A line that is exactly END marks the end of the document; anything after
it is ignored.

Any other line is a field: the first space separates KEY from VALUE. KEY
is everything before the first space; VALUE is everything after, with
surrounding whitespace trimmed. A line with no space is a field with an
empty value.

Field order is not significant. If a key repeats, the last occurrence
wins.

ENCODING

UTF-8. Line endings are not significant — a parser must accept both LF
and CRLF.

END
